{"type":"text","timestamp":1785872761357,"sessionID":"ses_031b5de68ffeW3IiUAK0XKmmr9","part":{"id":"prt_fce4f8852001fnWyHMs0JJ7cRj","messageID":"msg_fce4f77a0001Ik7jHXo1k4hG6n","sessionID":"ses_031b5de68ffeW3IiUAK0XKmmr9","type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what changed and the verification status.\n\n## Changed files\n\n1. **`app/api/data.js`** — new Vercel serverless function that mirrors the `leads.js` Blob pattern:\n   - `GET /api/data` reads the single dashboard blob (`data/dashboard-v1.json`) from Vercel Blob and returns the JSON database; returns `null` when the blob doesn't exist yet.\n   - `PUT /api/data` validates the body has a `settings` object, then writes the full database JSON back to the same Blob key.\n   - Returns clear errors and never throws unhandled.\n\n2. **`app/src/lib/store.tsx`** — wired the store to use `/api/data` as a cloud backup:\n   - Load path now tries, in order:\n     1. `VITE_API_URL` REST server if configured (unchanged behavior).\n     2. `/api/data` Vercel Blob endpoint otherwise.\n     3. Falls back to `localStorage`/seed if every network path fails.\n   - If the backend blob/server is empty, the current local data is seeded to it.\n   - The `/api/leads` merge now happens after the primary backend hydrate, so website leads are merged into the server-backed data rather than into local data that might later be overwritten.\n   - Persist path still writes to `localStorage` immediately, then debounces (500 ms) a `PUT` to either `${VITE_API_URL}/api/db` or `/api/data`.\n   - No exported hooks, types, or component interfaces changed.\n\n## Risks / caveats for reviewer\n\n- **Single shared blob key.** `data/dashboard-v1.json` is hard-coded. This is correct for a single-owner tool, but any future multi-user/tenant work must key by account.\n- **Vercel Blob is public.** Like `leads.js`, the blob is stored with `access: \"public\"`. The read/write token stays server-side, but the blob URL itself is world-readable if guessed. This matches the existing leads architecture.\n- **No merge conflict resolution.** The server blob wins on load. If Michael edits data on two devices offline, the last device to save will overwrite the other's changes. There is no CRDT or per-field merge.\n- **First-time seeding carries demo data.** On a fresh deployment with an empty blob, the store seeds it with whatever is in `localStorage` or `seed.ts`. The existing fake seed-data blocker (ASSISTANT_V1.md #3) is still present; this change just backs up whatever is currently in the app.\n- **Blob size limit.** The entire database is serialized as one JSON blob. Vercel Blob's limit is ~4.5 MB, which is ample for a small-business dashboard for a long time.\n- **No live integration test was run.** I verified syntax/module load with `node --check` and `import()`, but I did not exercise the live Blob token against real storage to avoid touching production data. The read/write pattern is copied directly from the already-working `leads.js`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run build` inside `app/` — **passes** (TypeScript + Vite production build clean).\n- `npm run verify` inside `app/` — **passes** (all 71 assistant/pricing checks pass).\n\nNo commit or push was made.","time":{"start":1785872746578,"end":1785872761353}}}
